.TH POWER4D 1 "August 1, 2026" "power4d" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
power4d \- collect reports from multiple power4 controllers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B power4d
.RB [ \-i | \-\-interval
.IR seconds ]
.RB [ \-b | \-\-baud
.IR rate ]
.RB [ \-o | \-\-output\-directory
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.I node
.RI [ node... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B power4d
periodically collects six JSON reports from each configured power4 controller:
.IR batteries ,
.IR banks ,
.IR relays ,
.IR inputs ,
.IR parameters ,
and
.IR logs .
Each node runs independently so an unavailable controller does not delay the
other nodes.  Reports for one node are requested sequentially over one
short-lived connection.
.PP
Successful reports are validated using the P4J1 byte count and SHA-1 checksum,
then atomically installed as
.RI output-directory / node / report .json.
A failed report leaves its previous file unchanged.
.SH NODE SPECIFICATIONS
.TP
.BI tcp: host : password-environment : directory
Connect to the authenticated TCP console on IPv4 port 4244.  The host may be a
numeric IPv4 address or hostname.  Hostnames are resolved once at startup and
remain cached until the service restarts.  The password is read from the named
environment variable and must contain 16 to 128 printable bytes.
.TP
.BI serial: device : directory
Open the serial device in raw 8N1 mode.  The final colon separates the node
directory, so the device path itself may contain colons.
Every serial path is checked at startup and must exist, resolve to a character
device, and be readable and writable.  A failure terminates startup with the
offending path in the diagnostic.
.PP
The directory is both the node name used in logs and one path component below
the output root.  It may contain ASCII letters, digits, dot, underscore, and
hyphen, but may not be dot, dot-dot, or contain a slash or whitespace.  Node
directories must be unique.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i , " " \-\-interval " " \fIseconds\fP
Start-to-start collection interval.  The default is 60 seconds and the minimum
is 2 seconds.  A TCP node's entire connect, authentication, and collection
cycle is limited to half of this interval.
.TP
.BR \-b , " " \-\-baud " " \fIrate\fP
Baud rate applied to every serial node.  The default is 115200.  USB CDC ACM
devices may ignore this advisory setting.
.TP
.BR \-o , " " \-\-output\-directory " " \fIpath\fP
Root output directory.  The default is
.IR /run/power4 .
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-\-verbose
Log escaped bytes sent and received.  Password values are never logged.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH SERIAL LOCKING
Serial nodes acquire
.BR flock (2)
with
.B LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB
and then apply
.B TIOCEXCL .
If either exclusion mechanism reports the device busy, that node is skipped
immediately and retried at its next interval.  The lock is held across all six
reports and released as soon as the cycle finishes or its transport fails.
.SH SYSTEMD CONFIGURATION
The Debian service reads
.IR /etc/default/power4d .
For example:
.PP
.RS
.EX
INTERVAL=60
BAUD=115200
OUTDIR=/run/power4
POWER4D_OPTIONS=
NODES="tcp:10.10.10.3:PW1:shed serial:/dev/serial/by-id/example:house"
PW1="controller password"
.EE
.RE
.PP
The package enables but does not initially start the service.  Configure at
least one node, then run:
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemctl start power4d.service
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/power4d
Systemd environment and node configuration.  Installed mode 0600 because it
may contain passwords.
.TP
.I /run/power4/
Default runtime output root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B power4d
exits nonzero for invalid configuration, missing passwords, an invalid or
inaccessible serial path, hostname-resolution failure, or an unusable output
root.  Per-node runtime failures are logged and retried without terminating the
daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR power4ctl (1),
.BR flock (2),
.BR termios (3)
.SH AUTHOR
Jim Studt <jim@studt.net>
